  font->init ();
  if (unlikely (!font_interp.interpret (*font))) { fini (); return; }
  ...
}
```

The issue is subtle. When `fontDicts.push()` is called, it calls `resize(len + 1)`. Inside `resize`, if `size > len`, it does `memset(arrayZ() + len, 0, (size - len) * sizeof(*arrayZ()))` to zero-initialize the new element.

But then `font->init()` is called AFTER `fontDicts.push()`. If `push()` succeeds but later `font_interp.interpret(*font)` fails, `fini()` is called which does `fontDicts.fini_deep()`. This calls `fini()` on each font dict, including the one where `init()` was called.

